        "problem": "${\\int }_{2}^{3}\\frac{t}{8}\\,\\text{d}t=$",
        "worked_solution": "Factoring the constant out of the integral, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{2}^{3}\\frac{t}{8}\\,\\text{d}t & =\\frac{1}{8}{\\int }_{2}^{3}t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2}\\,{|}_{2}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{16}\\cdot {t}^{2}\\,{|}_{2}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{16}({3}^{2}-{2}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{16}(9-4) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{16}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
